> Inspect the actual native actor/value architecture

This separate trace uses the source CartPole preset: four input coordinates, two64-wide tanh layers per actor/critic trunk and two actions. REINFORCE omits its critic; ACKTR retains manual pre-activation endpoints. Comparison reports show their critic-enabled variant. MountainCar in the entropy report instead uses two normalized inputs and three actions. The trace initializes its own store and does not alter training.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/a2c_network.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace n=dm::nn;namespace m=n::models;std::filesystem::create_directories("build");n::ParameterStore p(0),critic(1);n::Module network([&](const n::Tensor&x){auto path=m::BuildActorCritic(p,x,2,64);return n::concat({path.probs,n::expand_dims(path.value,1)},1);},"a2c source actor/value");n::ModelPlotOptions options;options.detail=n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;options.sizing.minimum_extent=2;options.sizing.max_planes=2;network.plot(n::zeros({1,4}),options).save_svg("build/a2c_network.svg");}
```
